# Go
vendor/*
go.sum

# The blanket `vendor/*` ignores above (PHP/Go convention) were silently swallowing this
# workspace's own Rust `[patch.crates-io]` sources — `vendor/candle-core-0.11.0-wasm-fix`
# (pre-existing) and `vendor/candle-transformers-0.11.0-wasm-fix` (this workspace's own
# patched forks, see root Cargo.toml's `[patch.crates-io]` section for why each exists) were
# never actually committed, meaning a fresh clone or CI would fail to build `hacienda-wasm`'s
# `ner-candle-wasm` feature at all. Un-ignore them explicitly — `vendor/*` (not `vendor/`)
# above is what makes this negation effective: negating a child cannot resurrect it if the
# parent directory itself was excluded.
!vendor/candle-core-0.11.0-wasm-fix/
!vendor/candle-transformers-0.11.0-wasm-fix/
# Locally-built @xberg-io/xberg-wasm (39MB compiled binary, not source) — built from the
# same jamon8888/xberg checkout the workspace already pins, with the two patches above
# applied via a local (uncommitted) edit to that checkout's own Cargo.toml, and ocr-wasm
# (native WASI Tesseract, requires a WASI SDK this app doesn't use — see the app's own
# tesseract-wasm bridge instead) dropped to avoid that toolchain dependency. Committed
# (not just the source patches) so `apps/hacienda-studio`'s `file:../../vendor/
# xberg-wasm-ner-fix` dependency resolves on a fresh clone without a ~17-minute rebuild.
# Drop this whole directory (and the package.json dependency pointing at it) once xberg
# publishes a release with the F16/F32 fix upstream.
!vendor/xberg-wasm-ner-fix/

